{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QVtAAiNVVo9v33PbRypNFw","type":"tool_result","content":"23:P1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_pair_rail_parts/part_01.py:477-486, with CHANGELOG.md:191.\n24-Problem: when the host's target triple is absent from the manifest, the code runs _apply_currency_policy before any payload is resolved or hashed.\n25-- With no override, currency_path is the PATH launcher. The result is status=compatible, path=launcher and sha256=\"\". _resolve_codex_bin then returns the launcher and it gets executed. Nothing was hashed, and the native payload was never resolved.\n26-- The manifest pins only aarch64-apple-darwin. So this route applies on every other host (Linux x86_64/arm64, Intel macOS, Windows). Before this delta it was the documented fail-CLOSED result triple_missing (\"unverifiable must not silently degrade\").\n27-- With CEO_PAIR_RAIL_CODEX_BIN set, the override gets no is_file() check on this route. A missing override path that has any @openai/codex package.json above it newer than 0.160.0 returns compatible. The subprocess then raises FileNotFoundError, which becomes CodexUnavailable and an advisory: fail-OPEN. This inverts \"inexistente = BLOQUEIA\" (the line 520 contract).\n28-- CHANGELOG [1.4.4] line 191 says \"The payload's sha256 is still computed and recorded\". That is false on this route.\n29-Who is affected: maintainer and reviewer checkouts only. Installs do not receive .claude/governance/, so for them the manifest is absent and the pin fails open as before. The kit refuses this route for the re-pass. Condition 9 declares only the broad version-only trust, not this route.\n--\n44:6. Also part_01.py:477-486: on triples absent from the manifest, the strict \"newer than manifest\" rule blocks the manifest's own version (0.160.0) and admits any newer one. There is no hash on that route for a same-version tamper to mismatch, so the strictness has no purpose. This folds into the P1 fix.\n45-\n46:VERDICT