{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Arjmz3NBtkgMdWbrSs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AvgWvZmAiw9umDUE1RCSWJ","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"PAYLOAD 24/34. Files: check_pair_rail.py becomes a facade over _lib/_pair_rail_parts; check_plan_edit.py now uses _lib/plan_paths; check_precompact_continuity.py becomes a facade over _lib/_precompact_parts; three new files: _contamination_inventory.py, _repin_guard.py and _restore_archive.py. The content is the same as rc payload 23. The GA conditions say only CONDITIONS-ga.md changed since the rc tag. I re-checked everything independently against the candidate tree. All checks were static reading; I had no shell, so nothing was executed.\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS CHECKED AGAINST THIS PAYLOAD (all true)\n- C5: _KERNEL_PATHS lists .claude/hooks/_lib/_pair_rail_parts/**/* (check_arbitration_kernel.py:315), cli_currency.py (:333) and plan_paths.py (:334). The precompact hook is not kernel, so _precompact_parts not being enrolled is consistent.\n- C7: all three entry points keep their paths, and their logic moves under .claude/hooks/_lib/. _pair_rail_parts is a kernel path.\n- C9/C10: the `compatible` status is reachable through this facade. It comes from part_01.py:553-571 and needs version >= 0.160.0 and newer than the manifest's package_version, with no hash. _resolve_codex_bin (part_01.py:583) and --verify-codex-pin (part_04.py:510) both accept `verified` or `compatible`. Adopters are not affected: .claude/governance/ is not installed (scripts/install.sh has no copy of it), so the manifest is unreadable, the result is infra, and the rail is advisory as before.\n- CHANGELOG.md:332-333 (FOLLOWUP plan names) and :342-346 (the new helpers ship to installs, ceo-restore.sh uses _restore_archive.py) match the code.\n\nMOVED-CODE VERIFICATION (no defect found)\n- _pair_rail_parts.install (__init__.py:8-24) rebuilds every function with the