  - Scenario: a fix to the read-back or ingress redaction applied only to part_02 silently does not ship.\n   - Fix: keep one copy.\n4. P2 — scripts/doctor.sh:1188 (rc codex P2, re-confirmed).\n   - Problem: the CEO_PAIR_RAIL_TIMEOUT_S default moved to part_03, so doctor's timeout coherence check now always prints a \"skipped\" NOTE.\n   - Scenario: an adopter whose registration timeout is below 210 s loses the warning that the harness can kill the 180 s review.\n   - Fix: read the default from part_03, or from the rebound main().\n5. P2 — plan_paths.py:34 returns filename[:8] (rc P2, re-confirmed).\n   - Problem: a followup plan's id collapses to its parent's.\n   - Scenario: check_plan_edit.py:161 emits plan_transition with the parent's id (PLAN-194) when a FOLLOWUP plan changes status.\n   - Fix: return or emit the full FOLLOWUP id.\n6. P2 — CHANGELOG.md:332 is incomplete.\n   - Problem: the new grammar (plan_paths.py:13-15) also stops matching names with double or trailing hyphens, which the old `[a-z0-9-]+` regex gated.\n   - Scenario: such plan files leave the lifecycle check without notice. This is fail-open, and PLAN-SCHEMA's kebab-case rule makes these names non-conforming.\n   - Fix: one CHANGELOG clause.\n7. P2 — docstrings and markers.\n   - Problem: check_precompact_continuity.py:45-47 still promises \"missing files → breadcrumb + emit {}\". A missing _lib/_precompact_parts now gives an import traceback and no {}.\n   - Problem: a missing _pair_rail_parts likewise gives no pair_rail_fatal_failopen breadcrumb.\n   - Problem: _precompact_parts/__init__.py:16 replaces the facade's __doc__ with the last part's docstring (rc P2).\n   - Fix: reword the docstrings, and restore __doc__ after install.\n8. P2 — _lib/_contamination/term_scan.py:12 imports .claude/scripts/_contamination_inventory by bare module name.\n   - Problem: that _lib module works only when .claude/scripts is on sys.path, which is true for check_contamination.py run directly; gen_envelope.py adds it by hand.\n   - Carried: _contamination_inventory.py:76 still fails on a core.symlinks=false checkout (codex rc).\n   - Fix: move the inventory module under _lib, or pass it in as a dependency.\n9. P2 — _restore_archive.py:44 (codex rc, carried).\n   - Problem: on Python 3.9, a GNU longname directory entry can keep its trailing slash. The split then yields an empty component and a valid long-path backup is refused. This is fail-closed.\n   - Fix: strip one trailing slash before validating the components.","decision":"GO","sentence":"Against the code in this payload, conditions 5, 7, 9 and 10 hold, the moved pair-rail and precompact code keeps its name lookup, patch points and fail directions, the new restore validator fails closed and writes only to its stage directory, and the only findings are P2 follow-ups plus a P1 that was already in the signed annex."}}}
